Information architecture 2026-09: Hero / Work / Ventures / Lab / Archive.

- Homepage: H1 "Physics-constrained intelligence for grids and traction
  power.", two-line promise, ONE paid CTA (€280 teardown), ONE live
  instrument (in-browser IEEE 9-bus DC power flow reproducing the explorer's
  analytical solution and its 4.44e-16 p.u. residual; N-1 trip control),
  exactly three proof chips. Seven synthetic canvases, carousels and the
  second commercial story removed from the homepage.
- New routes: /advisory (€280 door, €3,200 only after a teardown, pilot,
  scope boundaries), /network (four lines, one verb each), /ventures,
  /lab (parked; 404 GitHub paths rendered as text, never links), /books
  (pointer to grimaldi.ca/books). /work is now a gated register; /simulator
  carries the instrument, the residual table and "what this is not".
- Status vocabulary (app/lib/status.ts) on every artefact; linkable() gate
  for the five GitHub paths that 404 as of 2026-09-01.
- Validation numbers fetched from the explorer's report JSON at build /
  revalidate with a dated snapshot fallback (app/lib/validation.ts).
- New components: StatusBadge, HeroInstrument, ResidualTable, OfferCard,
  VentureShelf, NetworkFooter (exact four convergence lines).
- SEO: new title, Person + ProfessionalService + two Offers pointing at
  /advisory, llms.txt regenerated from the registry, sitemap re-ranked.
- verify.sh gains an honesty contract (no 404 GH links on / /work
  /simulator; homepage free of Peru / paint / orbital / banned phrases;
  H1 + SSR instrument present). CI axe + Lighthouse cover the new routes.
- All previous routes, locales (EN/ES/DE/ZH) and content kept; /de /es /zh
  redirects now honoured by the locale layer via ?lang=.

